          "topic": "AI深度访谈",
          "summary": "In this solo finale to his three-part series following two weeks in China, Nathan delivers a net assessment of Chinese AI capabilities and constraints ahead of dedicated US-China bilateral AI talks. He audits the impact of export controls, analyzes the perspective from Beijing, and outlines an actionable framework for a cooperative Pax Robotica. Nathan argues for joint compute initiatives, safety auditor standards, and conventions on autonomous weapons to keep tech trees entangled. Ultimately, he warns that pursuing an adversarial zero-sum race risks training frontier AI systems for conflict rather than the shared benefit of humanity.\n\nFor full show notes, links, and references, read the episode page:\nhttps://www.cognitiverevolution.ai/na...\n\nSPONSORS:\nDeepgram Flux TTS: Deepgram Flux TTS is a streaming text-to-speech model built for voice agents with natural tone, context awareness, and interruption handling. Try it free until September 12 at https://deepgram.com/keeptalking?utm_...\n\nClaude: Claude is the AI collaborator for problem solvers, helping with writing, coding, financial models, strategy, and more. Get started with Claude and explore Claude Pro at https://claude.ai/tcr\n\nCHAPTERS:\n(00:00) About the Episode\n(06:11) Episode intro and recap\n(08:56) The Pax Machina goal\n(12:32) The Anthropic worldview (Part 1)\n(16:50) Sponsors: Deepgram Flux TTS | Claude\n(18:55) The Anthropic worldview (Part 2)\n(18:56) Net assessment of China\n(32:26) China's eternal 1991\n(44:03) History of Chinese AI\n(54:34) China's domestic constraints\n(01:07:09) Century of humiliation narrative\n(01:27:01) Signs of Chinese cooperation\n(01:42:38) American state capacity lessons\n(02:05:39) Evaluating AI export controls\n(02:27:25) Hyperstitioning a summit deal\n(02:44:28) Preserving mutual legibility\n(03:01:12) Autonomous weapons convention\n(03:09:33) Positive sum AI competition\n(03:12:31) Episode Outro\n(03:15:05) Outro\n\nPRODUCED BY:\nhttps://aipodcast.ing\n\nSOCIAL LINKS:\nWebsite: https://www.cognitiverevolution.ai\nTwitter (Podcast): https://x.com/cogrev_podcast\nTwitter (Nathan): https://x.com/labenz\nLinkedIn:   / nathanlabenz  \nYoutube:    / @cognitiverevolutionpodcast  \nApple: https://podcasts.apple.com/de/podcast...\nSpotify: https://open.spotify.com/show/6yHyok3...",
